ContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"steinerTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"terminals"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SteinerTree","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees11SteinerTreeV","text":"SteinerTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">? "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","text":"AdditiveArithmetic"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"terminals","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices to connect.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"weight","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each edge’s weight, from its position."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tree’s edges, in position order, and their total weight.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One Dijkstra search from all terminals at once assigns every vertex to its nearest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"terminal. Each edge between two terminals’ regions joins them at the length of the path","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through it, a minimum spanning tree of those joins picks which regions to connect, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tree is the picked edges with the shortest paths from their ends to their terminals. Its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight is at most 2(1 − 1\/ℓ) times the optimum, where ℓ is the number of leaves of an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optimal tree. Every leaf is a terminal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Repeated terminals count once. With fewer than two terminals the tree has no edges. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge that is not a self-loop is weighed once; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" is not kept.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every terminal is a vertex; every weight is at least zero and not NaN; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path lengths do not overflow.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/steinerTree(terminals:weight:)"},"abstract":[{"text":"An approximate minimum Steiner tree connecting ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminals"},{"text":", by Mehlhorn’s algorithm; nil","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when two terminals are in different components.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/steinertree(terminals:weight:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SpanningTrees","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/SteinerTree":{"url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/steinertree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SteinerTree","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SteinerTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Steiner tree of an undirected graph: a tree among the graph’s edges that connects every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"terminal, through other vertices where that helps, as edge positions with their total weight."}],"title":"SteinerTree","role":"symbol","